---
// TERMS OF USE — for musacad.org. The application itself is governed by its
// license (LGPL-3.0-or-later), which these terms point to and never narrow.
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, FLATHUB_URL, LICENSE_URL, MAINTAINER, REPO_URL } from '../data/site';

const title = 'Terms of Use — Musa CAD Website, License and Downloads';
const description =
  'The terms for using musacad.org and downloading Musa CAD: the LGPL license, no warranty, official download sources, trademarks, donations and third-party tools.';
const crumbs = [{ name: 'Terms of use', path: '/terms/' }];
const UPDATED = '2026-10-04';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const mail = `mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`;
---

<Page {title} {description} {crumbs}>
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Terms" title="Terms of use" {crumbs} updated={UPDATED}>
    <p>
      These terms cover this website, musacad.org. The Musa CAD application is covered by its
      own license, the GNU LGPL — nothing here takes away any right that license gives you.
    </p>
  </PageHeader>

  <article class="prose-doc mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pb-28 sm:px-8">
    <h2 id="about-these-terms">About these terms</h2>
    <p>
      musacad.org is run by me, {MAINTAINER}. By using the site you agree to these terms. If you
      don’t agree, please don’t use it — you can still get Musa CAD and its source code from
      <a href={REPO_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="license">The software and its license</h2>
    <p>
      Musa CAD is free software, released under the
      <a href={LICENSE_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3 or later</a>.
      You may use it for any purpose, including commercial work, and you may study, change and
      share it under that license’s terms. The license, not this page, decides what you may do
      with the program; where the two ever seem to differ, the license wins.
    </p>
    <p>
      What you draw with Musa CAD is yours. The license covers the program, not your drawings.
    </p>

    <h2 id="no-warranty">No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      Musa CAD is provided <strong>as is, without warranty of any kind</strong>, as its license
      sets out. To the extent the law allows, I’m not liable for any loss or damage that comes
      from using it or this website — including lost or corrupted drawings, wrong dimensions,
      or costs that follow from them.
    </p>
    <p>
      CAD drawings often end up as buildings, parts and machines. Check your work, especially
      dimensions and anything converted from another format, before anyone builds from it, and
      keep backups of drawings that matter.
    </p>

    <h2 id="downloads">Official downloads</h2>
    <p>Official builds of Musa CAD come from three places only:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>this website,</li>
      <li>the releases of <a href={`${REPO_URL}/releases`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">MusaCAD/MusaCAD on GitHub</a>, and</li>
      <li><a href={FLATHUB_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Flathub</a>, as <code>org.musacad.MusaCAD</code>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Anyone may build and share Musa CAD under its license, but builds from anywhere else
      aren’t mine and I can’t vouch for them. Where a release publishes a SHA-256 checksum, use
      it to check your download.
    </p>

    <h2 id="third-party">Third-party software and services</h2>
    <p>
      Opening and saving DWG uses the ODA File Converter, a separate program by the Open Design
      Alliance, under its own license — you accept the Open Design Alliance’s terms when you
      download it. GitHub, Flathub, PayPal and Ko-fi are run by others under their own terms.
      AutoCAD is a registered trademark of Autodesk, Inc.; Musa CAD is an independent project
      and is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by Autodesk.
    </p>

    <h2 id="trademarks">The Musa CAD name and logo</h2>
    <p>
      The Musa CAD name and logo identify this project. You’re welcome to use them to talk about
      Musa CAD — in reviews, articles, tutorials and courses. Please don’t use them in a way that
      suggests your own product, service or modified build is Musa CAD or is endorsed by it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="donations">Donations</h2>
    <p>
      <a href={`${base}donate/`}>Donations</a> are voluntary gifts toward development. They don’t
      buy goods, services, support or influence over the project, and they’re processed by the
      payment service you choose, under its terms. If you sent one by mistake, write to me at
      <a href={mail}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="website">Using this website</h2>
    <p>
      Please don’t try to disrupt the site, its hosting, or anyone else’s use of it. Information
      here is offered in good faith and kept as accurate as I can, but it may be incomplete or
      out of date — the release notes and the documentation in the repository are the reference.
      The source of this website is public on
      <a href="https://github.com/MusaCAD/MusaCAD-Website" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="links">Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>
      This site links to services I don’t run. I’m not responsible for their content, their
      availability or their practices.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      If these terms change, this page changes with them and the date at the top moves. Every past
      version is in this website’s
      <a href="https://github.com/MusaCAD/MusaCAD-Website/commits/main/src/pages/terms.astro" target="_blank" rel="noopener">public history</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms: <a href={mail}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Page>
